    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Alongside the Matplotlib helpers, physicskit.chaos.visualizers.dynamic_plots provides interactive Plotly figures: a trajectory you can pan and zoom, and an interactive Poincare section you can hover over to inspect individual bounce points. The billiard used here is the Sinai billiard: a square cell, |x|\le L/2,\ |y|\le L/2, with a circular scatterer of radius r_s removed from its center, x^2+y^2=r_s^2, off of which the particle undergoes specular reflection, \mathbf{v}&#x27; = \mathbf{v} - 2(\mathbf{v}\cdot\mathbf{n}) \,\mathbf{n}, whenever it strikes the boundary.">

